pycoloc translates statistical algorithms and result conventions from coloc.

coloc 6.0.3, official commit 8f20f0bc5e60ffc99e4c2f787bd55fd30cfe7c45
https://github.com/chr1swallace/coloc
Upstream DESCRIPTION license: GPL (without a version restriction).
Upstream authors: Chris Wallace, Claudia Giambartolomei, Tom Willis,
Jeffrey Pullin; contributor Vincent Plagnol. Preserve their authorship of
the original methods and R implementations. Python adaptation is distributed
under GNU GPL version 3 or later; upstream licensing is not re-labelled.

Source files consulted: R/claudia.R, R/susie.R, R/check.R. Comments identify
Claudia Giambartolomei, Chris Wallace and Vincent Plagnol for core ABF functions.
The package includes no vendored susieR source code. Official susieR 0.16.6
(BSD 3-clause), commit 8e56a8e038e989856d106d9ca5175cc664fea9d2, is used
outside this package to produce the separately identified reference outputs.

NumPy, SciPy, pandas, matplotlib and optional Numba are separately distributed
dependencies under their respective licenses; no dependency source is vendored.

Optional gffutils supplies local annotation indexing under its own license.

Public teaching fixture: examples/data contains a portable conversion of the complete synthetic coloc_test_data D1-D4 from coloc 6.0.3 commit 8f20f0bc5e60ffc99e4c2f787bd55fd30cfe7c45. Attribution: Chris Wallace and coloc contributors. Its upstream unversioned GPL declaration and GPL-3 text are retained in examples/data/README.md, LICENSE.GPL-3 and upstream/coloc_DESCRIPTION. Frozen susieR0.16.6 reference outputs are separately identified by examples/data/reference.lock.json. No private study data are bundled.
